{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-141406",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $|r|=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThe given sequence ${a}_{n}={3}^{n}$ is a geometric sequence with the common ratio $r=3.$ \n\nSince $|r|>1,$ the sequence diverges.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
